History of Herding (c. 40-50 years ago, by Saffet Üstün of ﬁÖ) -
Agriculture was way behind herding. With horse and bull; no chemical fertilizer, no tractor..we used dung as fuel, not sufficient for fertilizer.  
Had lots of herds..Izzet a€a had 3 a€ıls; he had 600-700 sheep and more than 1,000 goats. Osman Ba€cı etc...village had more than 10,000..Now, at most 4,000..
Goat pop.: more than 10,000 in ﬁÖ.
We used goat for “kurban” (male); tiftik was cheap, sold it to tiftik cooperative in
Polatlı..I sold my goats to people from Manisa.
